A||N||5||JeffDm||Stiff manual shifting on '88||||5||
Z||000000||JeffDm||12-29-2000||10:12 AM||||I just bought an '88 coupe (2M4) with the manual transmission and it seems that the shifter is very stiff, much stiffer than my Grand Am which I was told has the same tranny & engine, although the Fiero is still shiftable.  Is there something that I should look for?  To be honest I haven't had a chance to open the rear lid to look inside.<P>I am just fishing for suggestions on what might be the most common causes on this particular kind of car.  I'll get thoughrough with the shop manual this evening too.<P>Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||ChadMan||12-29-2000||11:27 AM||||Well, something's screwy, because the Isuzu 5-sp is normally a pretty slick-shifting transmission.<P>Is it stiff going into all the gears, or just a couple?<P>First thing I'd do is check the transaxle fluid.  Replacing the mud in my 86 SE with fresh 5W-30 made a world of difference.  Next, check the cables - they may be worn out, or more likely have been improperly replaced and are out of adjustment.  Also, could your shifter be bent from some meathead prior owner slam-shifting it?<P>You didn't complain about the clutch, so I assume it is working properly.  If it wasn't disengaging all the way, that would certainly cause a problem like yours too!<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 12-29-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000002||FieroJoe||12-29-2000||11:57 AM||||possibly the owner before you had replaced the tranny oil, and used gear oil instead of motor oil.  There seems to be some people that are hell bent on putting gear oil in their manual transmissions, but it is definatly 5W-30.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||JeffDm||12-29-2000||12:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroJoe:<BR><B>gear oil in their manual transmissions, but it is definatly 5W-30.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I take it that the manual for the car truly recommends motor oil?  I haven't heard that one before.<P>Thanks for the comments.  We will definitely check the adjustments and linkages.  The amount of force to move the stick is equal for all gears.  I think we'll check the clutch adjustment too.  Unfortunately it will be a while before we can get the car inside.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever2||12-29-2000||07:10 PM||||Oh.  I've had the same symptom from my 88 4-cyl 5-spd Coupe since day-1, and have just been living with it.  Glad I saw this.<BR>(You mean now I actually have to get -under- the car?)<P><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000005||Jackalrr||12-29-2000||08:23 PM||||Make sure cables aren't bent around anything in the engine compartment.<P>Just my 2 cents  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>-Charlie<BR><P>------------------<BR>--------<BR>jackalrr@cinci.rr.com<P>85 GT 5spd<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fieroperformance.com/mycar21.jpg">  <BR>http://www.FieroPerformance.com||||reg||1
